From 6040b1c74c321407c442dad09d776b06d34e3db1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 05:02:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] qwen4exp: load upstream #29761 MTP GGUFs (nextn.hc_head_*
 mixer, QSA indexer in the MTP block, MTP-only files)

An upstream-converted Qwen3.8-Flash-Next GGUF could not be loaded at all, with or without MTP: its MTP block (blk.N)
carries blk.N.nextn.hc_head_{norm,down,up} and the block's QSA indexer tensors, which our loader never created, so the
tensor count check refused the file. An upstream MTP-only file also lacks the top-level output_hc_* mixer our sidecar
carries in that slot.

- llama-arch: LLM_TENSOR_NEXTN_HC_HEAD_{NORM,DOWN,UP} = blk.%d.nextn.hc_head_{norm,down,up}, same names and op info
  as upstream.
- loader: the MTP block creates nextn.hc_head_* (not required; our sidecar has none) and acknowledges the block's
  indexer tensors with TENSOR_SKIP (counted, never loaded: our MTP attention is dense, the indexer is dropped as in
  Strata mtp.cpp:215). An MTP-only file no longer requires the top-level output_hc_*.
- graph_mtp: the final mixer is nextn.hc_head_* when the file has it (an upstream full file's output_hc_* is the
  TRUNK's mixer), else output_hc_* (our sidecar). Asserts one exists.
- No math change: hnorm stays one RMS over all hc streams (SGLang qwen4_exp_mtp.py reference, QUESTIONS Q1/Q12);
  upstream's converter writes nextn.hnorm flat [hc*n_embd], the shape we already load. Our sidecar creates the same
  tensors and builds the same graph as before.

Port onto the v0.1.3.1 source tip (80cb4288de) of upstream-x1/port be19a79540, for the v0.1.3.2 served A/B.
Receipt (cells/rg7-summary.txt, RED fd9211c0c3 vs GREEN be19a79540): RED refuses up-full.gguf (expected 148, got 141)
and up-mtponly.gguf; GREEN CPU + Vulkan ids [92 109 18 22] equal to the sidecar, max|d|=0; sidecar logits FNV-1a
16d02dcc21b18fcc on both arms (bit-equal).

Taken-from: ggml-org/llama.cpp@c061df1983 (#29761) - tensor names and file layout only; the MTP math stays ours.
Measured-effect: upstream #29761 qwen4exp GGUFs (full and MTP-only) now load and draft with logits bit-equal to our
 sidecar of the same weights (CPU + Vulkan); our sidecar logits hash unchanged RED vs GREEN. Speed not measured
 (loader row). Served W5 MTP greedy ids-identical run on the real sidecar = cell p14ab (see MERGE-READY row P26).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
